WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.030
- Hi, I'm Meaghan from Khan Academy,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.910
and I'm here to share
more about the content

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.250
available on Khan Academy.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.020
When we talk about
content on Khan Academy,

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.830
what we really mean is
all the videos, articles

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.240
and practice questions that
learners interact with.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.720
We think about all of those
as split into two categories.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.740
The videos and articles
are instructional content,

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.510
and the practice questions
are practice content.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.560
Taken together, our goal
is to provide learners

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.700
with the ability to learn about anything

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.590
they might encounter in
a K through 12 classroom

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.540
and then practice what they've learned.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.490
A key part of that practice

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.400
is that they'll get instant feedback

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.683
about how they're doing.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.420
Along with work solutions to
help them get back on track

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.193
if they're not quite clear
on a particular concept.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.370
In this video we'll explain the content

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.700
we offer for teachers and students

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.223
and what makes it special.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.820
We know many people are familiar

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.270
with Khan Academy's great math content.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.470
But people are often unaware
that the Khan Academy

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.440
has more than math.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.400
People might be surprised to learn

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.420
that we've recently
launched a beta version

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.050
of our new English Language Arts content.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.930
Our goal is to eventually cover

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.073
all core academic subjects K through 14.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.640
We aren't there yet,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.800
but if you haven't explored beyond math,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.010
there are dozens of other courses

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.240
in the sciences, finance and economics

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.713
and arts and humanities.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.670
We also have test prep content

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.530
including free official SAT practice,

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.683
created in partnership with College Board,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.620
and official Praxis Core prep,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.423
developed in collaboration with ETS.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.720
We absolutely have not
forgotten about math though.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.730
We recently published a series
of Get ready for grade level

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.080
math courses for 3rd
grade to pre-calculus,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.333
to best prepare students
for on-grade level courses.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.440
If you are looking to learn something new,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.210
you can view all of our courses

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.800
by clicking the dropdown
menu in the top left

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.790
of the Khan Academy website.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.507
You can also find content to
support learning a new skill

00:02:10.507 --> 00:02:12.460
by using our search function

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:16.023
to search by skill name or by
Common Core State Standard.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.890
Khan Academy's content is
organized into courses.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.210
Most of our courses are divided into units

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.930
and within every unit
are multiple lessons.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.063
Lessons include instructional
and practice resources,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.600
such as videos, articles and exercises.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.240
In many courses quizzes combine practice

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.620
from several preceding lessons.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.070
Units end with a test
that checks understanding

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.403
of the entire unit.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.180
Khan Academy has a lot of
content created by a team

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.520
of former teachers and
subject matter experts.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.100
Our team ensures that all of
this content is high quality

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.280
by partnering with leading
educational organizations

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.240
and external experts to
make sure our content

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.530
is up to date and genuinely
aligned to standards.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.780
For math, in collaboration
with external reviewers,

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.850
we also tag all content
with regards to rigor

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.060
to be sure we are appropriately balancing

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.853
conceptual, procedural
and application content.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.300
As teachers we know you have many options

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.930
when it comes to using
tools in your classroom.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.857
So you might be asking yourself,

00:03:24.857 --> 00:03:28.240
"What makes Khan
Academy's content unique?"

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.660
Well, Khan Academy's
content is interactive.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.850
We have questions that
ask students to read

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.320
and interpret maps, images,
audio and text passages.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.150
We have interactive charts and graphs

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.490
to teach students to
read and interpret data

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.490
with a variety of
different question types.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.200
Consider exploring our
content to sample the variety

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.410
of practice questions we offer.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.120
Our content gives instant feedback.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.600
After answering any
question, students will learn

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.960
is they are corrects or incorrect.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.680
Students who are stuck on a problem

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.570
will be provided with support,

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:04.250
such as related videos and articles,

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.220
hints for solution strategies

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.090
and rationales that explain
why a particular answer

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.450
is correct or incorrect.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.160
We've heard some teachers
ask if Khan Academy's content

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.940
is student friendly.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.160
Our content is definitely
students friendly

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.060
and encourages a growth mindset

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:23.200
by letting students know
that they can learn anything.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.300
We want students to feel
like they're receiving

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.130
personalized support.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.380
We model thinking processes
that we hope students will use

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.773
as they ask questions and solve problems.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.510
We hope this video provides
a look into the content

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.570
available on Khan Academy.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.280
But we know the best way to
learn more is to experience it.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.983
Choose a topic that inspires
you and explore it firsthand.

